<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh rescues five Indian fishermen at sea.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh rescues five Indian fishermen at sea.</headline>
<dateline>COX'S BAZAR, Bangladesh 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladeshi fishermen rescued five crew of a wrecked Indian trawler in the Bay of Bengal on Thursday, police said.</p>
<p>They said the five were seen floating at high sea, some 100 km (60 miles) from Cox's Bazar coast, holding on to their battered vessel.</p>
<p>The Indians told the rescuers their trawler had been damaged and its engine stopped working in a storm last month. &quot;We survived by eating fish and water from the sea,&quot; one survivor told police at Cox's Bazar.</p>
<p>No other details were available.</p>
</text>
